+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a category currently deletes products that have no remaining category, breaking product details, carts, and orders. It can also leave category reads failing instead of returning the expected not-found response. Category deletion must be a catalog-structure operation that preserves product records and historical commerce data.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Delete only the selected category and all descendants.
+- Remove deleted categories from product associations while preserving products, inventory, pricing, and all non-deleted associations.
+- Keep carts and orders usable when they contain affected products.
+- Return HTTP 404 for deleted or nonexistent categories, and show no products when filtering by a deleted category.
+- Add regression coverage for root/descendant deletion, multi-category products, and cart/order references.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `category-deletion`: Category deletion removes catalog categories and associations without deleting products or commerce records.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+The category service and private category API are affected, along with product-category persistence and integration tests. Cart and order models/services should remain compatible because product entities are retained; tests must prove those flows remain readable and operable.
