+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Preserves catalog products and commerce history when merchants remove a category tree, while making the removed category tree consistently unavailable through the public catalog APIs.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Category deletion preserves products
+The system SHALL delete the selected category and its descendants without deleting associated products or changing their stock, price, or other category associations.
+
+#### Scenario: Product only belongs to deleted tree
+- **WHEN** a merchant deletes a category containing a product whose only categories are in that category tree
+- **THEN** the product remains retrievable by SKU with its stock and price unchanged and with no deleted categories listed
+
+#### Scenario: Product has another category
+- **WHEN** a merchant deletes a category tree containing a product that is also assigned to a category outside the tree
+- **THEN** the product remains retrievable and retains the outside category association
+
+### Requirement: Category descendants are removed as a tree
+The system SHALL delete every descendant of the selected category and remove all product associations to every deleted category.
+
+#### Scenario: Nested descendant deletion
+- **WHEN** a merchant deletes a category with nested child categories
+- **THEN** the selected category and all descendants are absent from category listings and no product is listed by any deleted category id
+
+### Requirement: Commerce references remain valid
+The system SHALL preserve carts and orders that reference products affected by category deletion.
+
+#### Scenario: Existing cart and order
+- **WHEN** a category containing a cart or order product is deleted
+- **THEN** the cart can still be read, changed, and checked out, and the order can still be opened
+
+### Requirement: Deleted category reads are not found
+The system SHALL return HTTP 404 Not Found for a deleted category or a category id that does not exist.
+
+#### Scenario: Read deleted category
+- **WHEN** a client requests GET `/api/v1/category/{id}` after deletion
+- **THEN** the API returns HTTP 404 Not Found
+
+#### Scenario: Delete missing category
+- **WHEN** a client requests DELETE `/api/v1/private/category/{id}` for a nonexistent id
+- **THEN** the API returns HTTP 404 Not Found
